{"created": "2026-11-15T02:16:49.983735+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-15T02:20:30.263946+00:00", "id": 24237543, "conceptrecid": "24237542", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24237543", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.24237542", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24237543", "metadata": {"title": "MARGINAL GROWTH RATES OF MATRIX PRODUCTS NEED NOT BE WEAKLY INCREASING OR REGULARLY VARYING", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24237543", "publication_date": "2026-11-15", "description": "<p>Let $\\mathcal{M}$ be a compact set of real square matrices with joint spectral radius one, and let $g(n)$ be the largest norm of a product of $n$ matrices from $\\mathcal{M}$. Varney and Morris asked whether $g$ is always weakly increasing and weakly upper regularly varying; this is Problem MF-11 of the collection Open Problems in Numerical Linear Algebra. We show that both properties can fail, even for pairs of matrices. We construct an explicit pair of real $20\\times20$ matrices, depending on a Liouville number $\\theta_\\star$, for which the ratios $g(N/2)/g(N)$ and $g(2N)/g(N)$ are unbounded along the lengths $N=16^{p}$ for which $p\\theta_\\star$ is extremely close to an integer. Both properties also fail for a pair of invertible matrices and for a pair of $22\\times22$ matrices with $n\\le g(n)\\le Cn(\\log n)^{2}$. On the other hand, both properties hold for every finite set of $3\\times3$ matrices, so that the smallest dimension of a counterexample lies between $4$ and $20$, and $g$ is weakly increasing for block triangular families with two product bounded diagonal blocks, one of which contains an elliptic product or is irreducible with a product of spectral radius one. The proofs reduce products to a seven-dimensional commutative nilpotent algebra, in which a quadratic term cancels exactly at certain lengths.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Pedro Martins", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0004-6254-6727"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "24237542"}}]}}, "title": "MARGINAL GROWTH RATES OF MATRIX PRODUCTS NEED NOT BE WEAKLY INCREASING OR REGULARLY VARYING", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24237543", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24237543", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24237543?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24237543", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24237543", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24237543", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24237543/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24237542", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24237542", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24237542", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24237542", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24237543/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24237543/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24237543/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24237543/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24237543:__TITLE____2_.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24237543:__TITLE____2_.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24237543:__TITLE____2_.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24237543:__TITLE____2_.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24237543:__TITLE____2_.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24237543:__TITLE____2_.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24237543/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24237543/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/ap